<Site title="Research method — Cadastre"><div class="shell page-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span>Research method</span></div><h1 class="sr-only">Research method</h1>      <section class="method-section surface-ink" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title"><div class="shell section-space"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / THE METHOD</p><h2 id="method-title">From a public source<br/>to a defensible reference.</h2></div><p class="method-intro">Extraction is the beginning. Provenance, explicit uncertainty, and review turn an image into evidence.</p></div><div class="method-grid"><article><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Collect with context.</h3><p>Discover public agency documents. Record their source URLs, publishing jurisdiction, retrieval metadata, and cryptographic fingerprints.</p><div class="step-tag">SOURCE → HASH → MANIFEST</div></article><article><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Extract without pretending.</h3><p>Preserve native images, text, vector references and their placements. Associate design-specific source statements and leave uncertain relationships for review.</p><div class="step-tag">EXTRACTION ≠ ACCEPTANCE</div></article><article><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Review before reference.</h3><p>Review depicted jurisdiction, document family, design generation, and geometry. Keep uncertain observations out of accepted cohorts.</p><div class="step-tag">EVIDENCE → REVIEW → COHORT</div></article></div><div class="metrology-note"><span class="note-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⊞</span><div><h3>Evidence appropriate to every claim.</h3><p>Sourced topology and tested computations can be published directly. ID-1 normalization supplies nominal coordinates. A claimed measurement tolerance or detection rate needs its own supporting evidence; physical-card collection is not a prerequisite for publishing the reference catalog.</p></div><a href="/schemas/cohorts.schema.json" class="text-link">Inspect the schema <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</Site>
